From acca51c321021ea169ff6d4adbf5899a38fc0285 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 11:46:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/23] can: isotp: add the frame transmission time to the CF
 broadcast gap

With flow control the gap between the consecutive frames is the frame
transmission time (N_As) plus the minimum separation time (N_Cs). N_Cs is
the STmin value from the received FC or the value of the
CAN_ISOTP_TX_STMIN socket option when the CAN_ISOTP_FORCE_TXSTMIN flag is
set.

In CAN_ISOTP_CF_BROADCAST mode there is no FC and the gap is set in
isotp_sendmsg(). With the CAN_ISOTP_FORCE_TXSTMIN flag only the value of
the CAN_ISOTP_TX_STMIN socket option is used and the frame transmission
time is missing.

Add the frame transmission time to the CF broadcast gap in both cases
like in the flow control mode and document the gap in iso15765-2.rst.

Additionally fix the unit of the values of the CAN_ISOTP_TX_STMIN and
CAN_ISOTP_RX_STMIN socket options in iso15765-2.rst. Both values are
handled in nanoseconds by the implementation, as documented in isotp.h.

Signed-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
---
 Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst | 9 ++++++---
 net/can/isotp.c                         | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst b/Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst
index 37ebb2c..badcd16 100644
--- a/Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst
+++ b/Documentation/networking/iso15765-2.rst
@@ -199,7 +199,10 @@ where the ``can_isotp_options`` structure has the following contents:
     specified alongside ``CAN_ISOTP_CF_BROADCAST``).
 
   * ``CAN_ISOTP_CF_BROADCAST``: use 1-to-N transmission without flow control
-    (cannot be specified alongside ``CAN_ISOTP_SF_BROADCAST``).
+    (cannot be specified alongside ``CAN_ISOTP_SF_BROADCAST``). The gap
+    between the consecutive frames is ``frame_txtime`` plus the value of the
+    ``CAN_ISOTP_TX_STMIN`` socket option when the ``CAN_ISOTP_FORCE_TXSTMIN``
+    flag is set.
     NOTE: this is not covered by the ISO 15765-2 standard.
 
   * ``CAN_ISOTP_DYN_FC_PARMS``: enable dynamic update of flow control
@@ -286,7 +289,7 @@ Transmission stmin
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
 The transmission minimum separation time (stmin) can be forced using the
-``CAN_ISOTP_TX_STMIN`` optname and providing an stmin value in microseconds as
+``CAN_ISOTP_TX_STMIN`` optname and providing an stmin value in nanoseconds as
 a 32bit unsigned integer; this will overwrite the value sent by the receiver in
 flow control frames:
 
@@ -299,7 +302,7 @@ Reception stmin
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
 The reception minimum separation time (stmin) can be forced using the
-``CAN_ISOTP_RX_STMIN`` optname and providing an stmin value in microseconds as
+``CAN_ISOTP_RX_STMIN`` optname and providing an stmin value in nanoseconds as
 a 32bit unsigned integer; received Consecutive Frames (CF) which timestamps
 differ less than this value will be ignored:
 
diff --git a/net/can/isotp.c b/net/can/isotp.c
index 8817f0e..7b88b3a 100644
--- a/net/can/isotp.c
+++ b/net/can/isotp.c
@@ -1292,11 +1292,11 @@ static int isotp_sendmsg(struct socket *sock, struct msghdr *msg, size_t size)
 		isotp_create_fframe(cf, so, ae);
 
 		if (isotp_bc_flags(so) == CAN_ISOTP_CF_BROADCAST) {
-			/* set timer for FC-less operation (STmin = 0) */
+			/* set timer for FC-less operation (N_As + N_Cs) */
+			so->tx_gap = ktime_set(0, so->frame_txtime);
 			if (so->opt.flags & CAN_ISOTP_FORCE_TXSTMIN)
-				so->tx_gap = ktime_set(0, so->force_tx_stmin);
-			else
-				so->tx_gap = ktime_set(0, so->frame_txtime);
+				so->tx_gap = ktime_add_ns(so->tx_gap,
+							  so->force_tx_stmin);
 
 			/* disable wait for FCs due to activated block size */
 			so->txfc.bs = 0;
-- 
